  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-285776" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training and Institutional Strengthening for Community Organisations and NGOs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) to encourage the sharing of experience and learning about community based economic initiatives and productive projects which strengthen the process of change towards a fairer and more equitable society in Latin America.

2) To offer holistic formation to members of civil society organisations throughout Latin America, with an emphasis on technical training, so that they can contribute to institutional strengthening in their own organisations.

3) To promote reflection upon  the socio-economic and political environment and upon traditional cultural values so that change agents trained through ICI courses can work to develop, strengthen and foster a sense of Latin American identity.

4) To encourage gender awareness at an institutional level and promote a Latin America wide gender perspective through ICI&apos;s educational processes as a contribution towards establishing real participatory and democratic practices in civil society organisations

5) To stimulate and encourage discussion about the role of community-based organisations in society, so that citizens can reclaim responsibility in the construction of a real democracy.

6) To link the current model of development with activities that contribute towards environmental degradation, and to strengthen organisational capacity in order to develop activities and ways of working which are environmentally sound.</narrative>
  </description>
